<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amazing Grace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">written late <a href="/years/1772">1772</a>, probably first used 1 January <a href="/years/1773">1773</a>; first printed <a href="/years/1779">1779</a> in Olney Hymns</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-newton">John Newton</a> was born in Wapping, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, in 1725 and went to sea at eleven. Pressed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>, he deserted, was traded as crew to a slave ship and took up slave trading. For a time he was himself enslaved by the Sherbro people of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> and forced to work on a plantation.</p></div>
